  "description": "Curtain Call: The Hits is the first greatest hits album by the American rapper Eminem. It was released on December 6, 2005, under Shady Records, Goliath Artists, Aftermath Entertainment, WEB Entertainment, and Interscope Records. The album collects Eminem's most popular singles, as well as three new songs: \"Fack\", \"When I'm Gone\", and \"Shake That\" featuring Nate Dogg. A live version of \"Stan\" performed with English singer-songwriter Elton John at the 43rd Grammy Awards is also included as a bonus track.",
